version 0.14.0
schematic main

# A 3.3 V rail and the sense line that measures it at the far end of the board. The schematic keeps
# the two nets apart -- they are different nets, with different members -- and the board joins them
# with copper. The join is the point: it changes the connectivity of both nets, so it has to be
# declared (spec/pcb.md §4.12) and it has to show up in the report.
#
# The two nets carry the same window on purpose: they are the same voltage, which is exactly what
# the tie says physically.
#
# There is no net-tie *part* here: the construction vocabulary is closed and has no entry for one
# (spec/teda.md §6.2.1), so the tie is the copper between two pads plus the declaration.
modules
  M1  tie-board

nets
  GND:         M1.GND
  V3V3:        M1.V3V3
  V3V3_SENSE:  M1.V3V3_SENSE
  VIN:         M1.VIN

ports
  GND         GND
  V3V3        V3V3
  V3V3_SENSE  V3V3_SENSE
  VIN         VIN

constraints
  voltage  GND         0V..0V
  voltage  VIN         4.5V..5.5V
  voltage  V3V3        3.135V..3.465V
  voltage  V3V3_SENSE  3.135V..3.465V
